# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for false vptr reports.
#
# A std::shared_ptr control block made in one shared library and released in
# another fails the vptr check: our libraries build with hidden visibility and
# libstdc++ is not built with UBSan, so each side has its own type info for
# the same control block type, and UBSan reports "does not point to an object
# of type '_Sp_counted_base'" (seen with GCC 12.1 for std::filesystem
# iterators and for shared_ptr<SpillCharge>). The object is valid; ASan and
# Valgrind report nothing there. GCC's UBSan matches the pattern against the
# mangled type name.
vptr_check:*_Sp_counted*
